SUMMARY:Interfaith Dinner: Día de Muertos
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261103T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261103T191500
DTSTAMP:20261102T204148Z
UID:dartmouth-groups-1632003@free-food-dartmouth
SEQUENCE:0
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Original event page(s):\nhttps://dartmouthgroups.dartmouth.edu
 /rsvp_boot?id=1632003\n\nDescription:\nIn partnership with the Tucker Cent
 er and Aquinas House\, LCHC will close the 2026 celebration with an interf
 aith dinner reflecting on Día de Muertos.\nThe evening will explore the c
 ultural significance of remembrance\, community grieving\, and honoring th
 ose who came before us. Through shared food\, reflection\, and interfaith 
 dialogue\, participants will consider the many ways communities remember\,
  grieve\, celebrate\, and carry traditions forward.\nRooted in remembrance
  and connection\, the dinner invites us to consider how different traditio
 ns can create opportunities for understanding and solidarity across commun
 ities.\n\nSponsor / organizer: Office of Pluralism and Leadership\n\nSourc
 e: Dartmouth Groups\n\nWhy this was included: Free Food category\; food or
  meal keyword in title\n\nFood availability is inferred from the source li
 sting\; verify details before attending.
