 nt?event=83161\n\nDescription:\nFirst presented in 2022 and dedicated to D
 artmouth\, the program also includes Dartmouth-inspired premieres.\nPavel 
 Lion (a.k.a. Psoy Korolenko)\, sometimes described as a “wandering schol
 ar” and an “avant-bard\,” is a multilingual singer-songwriter\, tran
 slator\, and lecturer. His programs typically combine original songs and t
 ranslations with works by other authors and his own renditions of traditio
 nal songs in Yiddish\, Russian\, Ukrainian\, Hebrew\, English\, French\, a
 nd Portuguese.\nThis concert will feature\, more extensively than usual\, 
 Psoy's original Russian-language songs translated into English\, as well a
 s songs by other authors in his own English translations.\n\nSponsor / org
 anizer: Jewish Studies Program\n\nAudience: Public\n\nSource: Dartmouth\n\
